# Cline / Roo Code Rules for Google Docs & Sheets Integration

When asked to inspect, read, or edit Google Docs or Google Sheets:
- Use the terminal tool with the global `gdoc` / `gsheet` CLI.
- Global authentication is pre-configured at `~/.gdoc/`.
- Every modifying action automatically creates a backup snapshot copy in Google Drive.

Key Commands:
- Read Doc: `gdoc read "<URL>"`
- Replace Text: `gdoc replace "<URL>" --find "<OLD>" --replace "<NEW>"`
- Append Text: `gdoc append "<URL>" --text "<TEXT>"`
- Read Comments: `gdoc comments "<URL>"`
- Reply to Comment: `gdoc reply "<URL>" --comment-id "<ID>" --text "<REPLY>"`
- Inspect Sheet: `gdoc sheet-info "<URL>"`
- Read Sheet: `gdoc sheet-read "<URL>" [--range "Sheet1!A1:D20"] [--json]`
- Update Cell: `gdoc sheet-update "<URL>" --range "Sheet1!B2" --values "Val"`
- Append Row: `gdoc sheet-append "<URL>" --values "Val1, Val2, Val3"`
